<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:04:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany's Merz arrives in Kyiv to pledge more support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c19a5c2824a2a6dd011ec84e776e7c2e7c8851f866999704f2feec96058b5bd</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:04:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T05:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-arrives-in-kyiv-to-pledge-more-support/a-79534734--46e2476f0408.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-arrives-in-kyiv-to-pledge-more-support/a-79534734?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz is expected to announce a new raft of measures to support Ukraine, including military aid and plans for the joint production of interceptor drones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Reform row raises fears for Merz's coalition</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c54869e81c3f55c358b91339b4ac5ee9c27517b7574772fe591879ebbde5c529</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-reform-row-raises-fears-for-merz-s-coalition/live-79512757--9a7ffc72b3eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-reform-row-raises-fears-for-merz-s-coalition/live-79512757?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's conservatives are dialing up the pressure on their center-left partners ahead of crunch talks next week. Meanwhile, Volkswagen's latest cost-cutting push has triggered a furious response.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>On German Unity Day, Steinmeier laments 'bitter setbacks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2d687f655a34a034afb0d4f304180c0a58b9dc62d91f71e64dc6dbb24e614c0</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T10:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-german-unity-day-steinmeier-laments-bitter-setbacks/live-79528092--4d5945f39bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/on-german-unity-day-steinmeier-laments-bitter-setbacks/live-79528092?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's president has used his final Unity Day speech to warn the hopes of the reunification era have suffered "bitter setbacks." DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German reunification: How inequality is shaping a new East German identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4cc0990f35cee2556df1d65431f2c1e055bb0f3241e24fb34f620a4fb22d68f</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T04:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-reunification-how-inequality-is-shaping-a-new-east-german-identity/a-79518541--28106a765624.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-reunification-how-inequality-is-shaping-a-new-east-german-identity/a-79518541?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new study highlights persistent structural disparities in wealth and leadership positions between East and West Germany, 36 years after reunification.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>ARD-Deutschlandtrend survey: Germans unite in frustration over the government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:507b83aa7e0e9d3c4eb1259cc623e0b16fbcfbd1baf6dfef7c8bc7b8b5901737</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ard-deutschlandtrend-survey-germans-unite-in-frustration-over-the-government/a-79515172--1741214668c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ard-deutschlandtrend-survey-germans-unite-in-frustration-over-the-government/a-79515172?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On the 36th anniversary of reunification, Germans are dissatisfied with the country's political leaders. They don't believe they'll be able to handle the challenges posed by AI, Russia and Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wins first game as Germany coach, without 'top dogs'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d68e616aab0f56ae957eb5071994a0b7620bd99d6c4774bc4f627b64b1f9ffb8</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898--6c1fca750e8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It may have taken a little longer than he would have liked, but Jürgen Klopp has finally won a game as Germany coach. Despite a number of debutants, it was a familiar face who stood out in the victory over Serbia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
